From f5b530503d01b9245bd62dc64b7db4ebda3a2030 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Ren=C3=A9=20Rebe?= <rene@exactco.de>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 00:40:10 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 01/35] m68k: Add NeXT Computer, NeXTcube and NeXTstation
 support
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Add a new machine type for the NeXT 68030 and 68040 systems.

 - head.S maps I/O space to 0xf0000000 with page tables, since RAM starts
   at physical 0x04000000 and its direct mapping can overlap the physical
   I/O addresses, ruling out transparent translation
 - 68040 models reach most devices through the BMAP I/O window
 - the 32 interrupt status and mask bits become a chained IRQ chip on the
   seven autovectors; some sources cannot be masked in hardware
 - system tick from the hardclock, clocksource from the 1 MHz event counter
 - reset re-enters the boot ROM with address translation off
 - the Z8530 platform devices move from the Mac code to shared setup code

"make nextboot" builds an OMAGIC a.out which the boot ROM loads over TFTP
or from disk.  The loader places the kernel ELF at the start of RAM and
builds bootinfo from the ROM mon_global, whose pointer is found in the ROM
vector table.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: René Rebe <rene@exactco.de>
---
